# DraftPolicy-2 (lane DraftPolicy, 2026-11-01; HuntDrafter F10, after waves 6e / 6e3): TF_GLM_DRAFT_EDGE=E@N, the DFlash2
# chain's selector edge weight E only in rounds where at least N streams decode, the recipe's 0.6 below; "E" alone
# (DraftPolicy-1's form) is E@1, every round. Measured split (6e / 6e3, engine-side): a lower weight drafts fewer rows
# at slightly fewer tokens a round, which wins where rows share a window (P4-P8) and loses fork texts 0-1 at 1-2
# streams. Lane DraftPolicy's replay WITH copy drafts (it reproduces every live forks cell of every fnc boot) puts the
# gate at 3: N = 2 loses the forks' P2 (rounds of 2 streams), N = 4 leaves the wave tails' 3-stream rounds (22% of
# P4's agent stream-rounds) on 0.6. Unset: (0.6, 1), the same float in every round: picks, confidences and replies
# bit-identical to the base. Any value: replies identical by construction (drafts are verified).
# The stream count is the round's decoding lanes (multi.MultiDecoder._round: DraftRequest.streams = len(lanes), the
# count TF_GLM_MULTI_DEPTH=scale uses); a solo drafter (P1, Drafter.propose) is one stream. Both ranks compare the gate
# at startup; draft_dump records the weight its (one-stream) chain used.
# Test: work/hunt/DraftPolicy/test_draft_edge2.py (CPU); mutants: mutants2.py.
# Applies with `patch -p0` in the folder holding tensorfold/, at the end of stack/all6x.list.
